{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>יכסימו.</b> Like יְכַסּוּם — and the middle yod is superfluous in it; and the way of Scripture is with this, like ״וְצֹאנְךָ יִרְבְּיֻן״ (Deuteronomy 8), ״יִרְוְיֻן מִדֶּשֶׁן בֵּיתֶךָ״ (Psalms 36) — and the first yod, which conveys future tense, thus interpret it: they sank in the Sea of Reeds so that the waters would return and cover them. יְכַסְיֻמוּ — there is nothing like it in Scripture in its vocalization, and its way is to be pointed יְכַסְיֻמוֹ מְלָאפוּם." "<b>כמו אבן.</b> And elsewhere: ״צָלְלוּ כַּעוֹפֶרֶת״, and elsewhere: ״יֹאכְלֵמוֹ כַּקַּשׁ״ — the wicked are like straw, tossed and blown, rising and falling; the middling are like stone; and the worthy are like lead, which sinks immediately (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "מְלָאפוּם is obscure; rendered as written. Likely a technical masoretic term, possibly related to 'full' pointing, but its precise meaning is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:24.932542387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}